-- dispatch (core): the positive half of A.54's gate. A `foreign type` IS
-- orderable when its own module declares a `pub compare` whose first
-- parameter is that type (A.50), and a shape holding one inherits it.
--
-- The control for `check/bad/core/CompareOnForeignWithUnrelatedCompare`,
-- which is the same file with `Handle` swapped out of the annotation: there
-- the gate must refuse, here it must accept — and the part it emits is the
-- call the module rule would make.
pub foreign type Handle


pub compare : Handle, Handle -> Order
compare a b = LT


pub before : ( Handle, Int ), ( Handle, Int ) -> Bool
before a b = a < b
